 "coverage": [
  "The 66667 nm rung of the guarded ladder is NOT taken: 50000 already refuses and a COARSER lattice carries a LARGER guard band, so it could only refuse too.  Every FINER rung IS taken.",
  "screen_bond_site_deficit's ladder ends at 0.250 mm: below that a barrel cannot carry a hole and the 0.125 mm annular ring at once, and the report names that floor rather than printing a zero-drill rung as a measurement.",
  "The lateral jumper is measured at the netclass 0.300 mm rung on the post-route board.  A --floors rung at 0.200 mm / 50000 nm was started and is NOT included; nothing in finding 6 depends on it, because PP3 does not price a jumper as a bond at any width."
 ],
 "edge": {
  "dst": [
   "J8.3"
  ],
  "note": "the Qwiic / STEMMA QT connector SDA contact -- a Demo-REQUIRED feature (AQROOT_DEMO_SCOPE.md)",
  "src": [
   "TP45.1",
   "J5.4",
   "R48.2",
   "D2.4"
  ]
 },
 "findings": [
  "1. THE GUARDED CORRIDOR IS A WALL AT EVERY PITCH, AND NOW IT IS MEASURED.  D-641's prose says the single-tube guard refuses at 100000, 50000 and 25000 nm; its evidence file records that arm at 100000 ONLY -- the 50000 and 25000 arms in it carry the FIFTY-tube guard.  All four rungs are now taken with the C4.2<->U3.12 tube ALONE -- 100000 (D-641), 50000, 33333, 25000 -- and every one is NO_PATH.  33333 nm is exactly the rung at which D-625's BTN_DOWN_N flipped from NO_PATH to ROUTES under the SAME tube, so `a refusal under a reservation is a refusal at a pitch` is TRUE for one net and FALSE for the other, and only the ladder tells them apart.",
  "2. THE BARREL ROAD IS NOT NARROW, IT IS EMPTY.  On the fragment THIS route creates, screen_bond_ladder's sites_in_fragment is 0 in all fifteen (pitch x barrel) cells, and the new screen_bond_site_deficit.py continues the DIAMETER ladder past every floor this board publishes: 0.600/0.200, 0.500/0.200, 0.450/0.200, 0.400/0.150, 0.350/0.100 and 0.300/0.050 all return ZERO sites in the fragment while the same rungs hold 95, 166, 215, 279, 390 and 486 in the ISLAND.  The verdict is NO_BARREL_AT_ANY_DIAMETER_ON_THIS_LADDER: no licence can buy this, because there is no diameter at which it exists.",
  "3. AND THE WHOLE OF IT IS TWO NAMED TRACKS ON TWO LAYERS.  Of the fragment's 1885 lattice cells at 0.050 mm, In1.Cu and In4.Cu admit 1697 each, hole-to-hole admits all 1885, In2.Cu 920, F.Cu 601, B.Cu 452 -- and In3.Cu just 111.  In3.Cu ALONE refuses 55 cells every other term admits and F.Cu ALONE refuses 5, and the objects are ONE /09_COMMUNITY_HEADER/TCA4307_READY track on In3.Cu (55 cells, 49.2-50.0 x 78.0-78.9 mm) and ONE /01_POWER_TREE/BAT_PROTECTED_P track on F.Cu (5 cells).  D-641 asked whether U3 is the thing that moves.  It is not: SIXTY legal 0.500/0.200 barrel sites in U3.12's own fragment are held by two tracks, one of them on the I2C buffer's own READY net.",
  "4. THE RE-BOND IS REFUSED AS A CORRIDOR, NOT AS A VIA SITE.  The plane repair's residual join -- the fallback maze3d's own doctrine names U3.12 for by name -- DOES run, and reports NO_PATH rather than NO_VIA_SITE: src_escapes 2 at 0.300 mm / 100000 nm, 8 at 0.200 mm / 100000 nm and 5 at 0.200 mm / 50000 nm, against 77, 92 and 55 destinations.  The pad escapes; the board offers nowhere to take it.",
  "5. THE LATERAL JUMPER WAS NEVER OFFERED TO THE REPAIR, AND U3.12'S FRAGMENT IS THE ONLY ONE OF THE FOUR ORPHAN GND CLUSTERS THAT COULD TAKE ONE.  route_maze_batch withholds --join-islands from the repair child (`a lateral jumper across a pour cut somewhere else on the board is a second transaction wearing a repair's name`) -- a reading that is right for a PRE-EXISTING orphan and wrong for the fragment the run itself made.  Asked directly on the post-route board, join_islands reports J3.A12/B1, MK1.4 and U9.16 NO_ANCHOR (`no cell of this cluster's filled copper admits a 0.300 mm track centred 0.250 mm inside it`) and U3.12 NO_PATH -- it is the one cluster whose copper could hold a jumper at all.",
  "6. AND NONE OF IT WOULD HAVE BEEN ENOUGH.  PP3 prices a fragment BONDED only where a BARREL of its own net lands inside a filled zone on a RESERVED INNER PLANE, so a jumper is not a bond however well it routes; and PP2 admits a split only when the net carries a published rail current, which GND -- a return plane -- does not (published_amps: null; .kicad_dru section 5 prices nine classes and none of them is GND).  EVERY split of a multi-pad GND island on this board is therefore refused UNCONDITIONALLY, whatever the router does.  The Qwiic SDA edge has THREE independent walls and the third is a CONTRACT.  The only promotable EXT_SDA route is one that does not split island 31 at all -- which is finding 1."
 ],
